              "children": [
                {
                  "id": "lede",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "When trailer brake lights stop working, it's more than just an inconvenience. Faulty trailer lighting creates serious safety risks on the road, increases the chance of accidents, and can lead to DOT violations that cost time and money. For owner-operators and fleet managers, electrical issues can quickly turn into expensive downtime if they are ignored for too long.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full",
                    "anchor": "post-lede"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-intro-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "At <a href=\"/locations/trailer-sales\">Sun State Trailers</a>, we understand that your trailer needs to stay road-ready every day. Whether you're hauling locally across Florida or making long-distance runs, dependable lighting systems are critical for safety, compliance, and protecting your business. If your trailer brake lights are not working, here's what may be causing the issue and why fast trailer repair matters.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-common-reasons",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Common Reasons Trailer Brake Lights Stop Working",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "common-reasons"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-common-reasons-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Brake light problems can come from several different areas within the trailer's electrical system. Some issues are simple, while others require professional diagnostics and repair.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h3-common-reasons-2",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Faulty Semi Trailer Electrical Connector",
                    "headingLevel": 3,
                    "align": "left"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-common-reasons-3",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "One of the most common causes of trailer brake lights not working is a damaged or loose semi-trailer electrical connector. The connector links the trailer's electrical system to the truck, allowing power to flow to the brake lights, turn signals, and running lights.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-common-reasons-4",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "<strong>Over time, connectors can experience:</strong>",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "cards-common-reasons-5",
                  "type": "row",
                  "props": {
                    "gap": 4
                  },
                  "styles": {
                    "base": {
                      "marginBottom": 20
                    }
                  },
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "id": "cards-common-reasons-5-1",
                      "type": "column",
                      "props": {
                        "span": 6
                      },
                      "styles": {
                        "base": {
                          "borderWidth": 1,
                          "borderStyle": "solid",
                          "borderColor": "line",
                          "paddingTop": 22,
                          "paddingRight": 22,
                          "paddingBottom": 22,
                          "paddingLeft": 22
                        }
                      },
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "id": "cards-common-reasons-5-1-list",
                          "type": "prose-list",
                          "props": {
                            "ordered": false,
                            "items": [
                              {
                                "text": "Corrosion"
                              },
                              {
                                "text": "Bent pins"
                              }
                            ]
                          }
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "id": "cards-common-reasons-5-2",
                      "type": "column",
                      "props": {
                        "span": 6
                      },
                      "styles": {
                        "base": {
                          "borderWidth": 1,
                          "borderStyle": "solid",
                          "borderColor": "line",
                          "paddingTop": 22,
                          "paddingRight": 22,
                          "paddingBottom": 22,
                          "paddingLeft": 22
                        }
                      },
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "id": "cards-common-reasons-5-2-list",
                          "type": "prose-list",
                          "props": {
                            "ordered": false,
                            "items": [
                              {
                                "text": "Moisture damage"
                              },
                              {
                                "text": "Loose wiring"
                              },
                              {
                                "text": "Dirt and debris buildup"
                              }
                            ]
                          }
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-common-reasons-6",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "If the connection becomes unstable, the trailer may lose brake light function completely or intermittently.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h3-common-reasons-7",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Damaged Wiring",
                    "headingLevel": 3,
                    "align": "left"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-common-reasons-8",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Electrical wiring on trailers takes a beating from road conditions, weather exposure, and constant vibration. Wires can become frayed, disconnected, or pinched over time.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-common-reasons-9",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "<strong>Damaged wiring may lead to:</strong>",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "list-common-reasons-10",
                  "type": "prose-list",
                  "props": {
                    "ordered": false,
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "text": "No trailer brake lights"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Flickering lights"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Intermittent brake light failure"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Blown fuses"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Short circuits"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-common-reasons-11",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Electrical issues are not always visible during a quick walkaround inspection, which is why routine trailer repair and inspections are important.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h3-common-reasons-12",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Burned-Out Bulbs or LED Failures",
                    "headingLevel": 3,
                    "align": "left"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-common-reasons-13",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Sometimes the issue is as simple as a failed light bulb or damaged LED assembly. While newer LED systems tend to last longer, they can still fail due to moisture intrusion or electrical overload. Checking light assemblies regularly should be part of every trailer maintenance routine.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h3-common-reasons-14",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Grounding Problems",
                    "headingLevel": 3,
                    "align": "left"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-common-reasons-15",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Poor grounding is another major cause of semi trailer brake lights not working. If the electrical ground connection is weak or corroded, power may not flow properly through the lighting system. Grounding issues often create inconsistent lighting behavior that can be difficult to diagnose without professional electrical testing.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "fig-1",
                  "type": "image",
                  "props": {
                    "width": "full",
                    "image": {
                      "src": "/img/blog/trailer-brake-lights-not-working/1.jpg",
                      "width": 1280,
                      "height": 853,
                      "alt": "Technician sitting on a trailer tailgate logging inspection notes on a clipboard"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-warning-signs",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Warning Signs of Trailer Electrical Problems",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "warning-signs"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-warning-signs-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Sometimes electrical issues appear before the brake lights fail completely. Catching these signs early can help prevent breakdowns and safety issues.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-warning-signs-2",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "<strong>Watch for:</strong>",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "checks-warning-signs-3",
                  "type": "check-list",
                  "props": {
                    "mark": "bullet",
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "text": "Flickering trailer lights"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Dim brake lights"
                      },
                      {
