                {
                  "id": "h-never-ignore",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Why Brake Light Problems Should Never Be Ignored",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "never-ignore"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-never-ignore-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "It may seem tempting to delay repairs when you're busy trying to keep loads moving, but brake light problems can create much bigger issues if left unresolved.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h3-never-ignore-2",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Safety Risks on the Road",
                    "headingLevel": 3,
                    "align": "left"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-never-ignore-3",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Brake lights alert drivers behind you when slowing or stopping. Without properly functioning brake lights, rear-end collisions become far more likely, especially during poor weather or nighttime driving. Proper lighting plays a major role in reducing those risks.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h3-never-ignore-4",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "DOT Violations and Fines",
                    "headingLevel": 3,
                    "align": "left"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-never-ignore-5",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Commercial trailers are required to meet federal lighting standards. During inspections, faulty brake lights can result in violations, citations, or even out-of-service orders. Unexpected downtime affects delivery schedules, customer relationships, and revenue.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h3-never-ignore-6",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Electrical Damage Can Spread",
                    "headingLevel": 3,
                    "align": "left"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-never-ignore-7",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Small electrical problems often grow into larger system failures over time. A damaged semi-trailer electrical connector or exposed wire can eventually affect additional lighting systems, ABS functions, or trailer components. Addressing problems early helps prevent more expensive trailer repair later.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "fig-2",
                  "type": "image",
                  "props": {
                    "width": "full",
                    "image": {
                      "src": "/img/blog/trailer-brake-lights-not-working/2.jpg",
                      "width": 1280,
