                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-road-ready",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Keep Your Trailer Road-Ready",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "road-ready"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-road-ready-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Electrical problems rarely fix themselves. At <a href=\"/locations/trailer-sales\">Sun State Trailers</a>, our parts and service team helps customers diagnose trailer lighting issues quickly so they can get back on the road with confidence.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-preventive",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Preventive Maintenance Helps Reduce Electrical Problems",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "preventive"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-preventive-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "One of the best ways to avoid lighting failures is by following a regular trailer maintenance schedule. Electrical inspections should always be part of a complete preventive maintenance program.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-preventive-2",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "<strong>Routine inspections should include:</strong>",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "list-preventive-3",
                  "type": "prose-list",
                  "props": {
                    "ordered": false,
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "text": "Checking the semi-trailer electrical connector"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Inspecting wiring harnesses"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Testing brake lights and signals"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Cleaning electrical contacts"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Checking ground connections"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Inspecting light housings for moisture"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-preventive-4",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Consistent maintenance helps reduce unexpected failures and keeps your trailer compliant with DOT standards.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-schedule-pro",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "When to Schedule Professional Trailer Repair",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "schedule-pro"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-schedule-pro-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Some lighting issues are easy to spot, but many electrical problems require professional diagnostics. Modern trailer electrical systems can become complicated, especially when wiring damage or hidden shorts are involved.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-schedule-pro-2",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "<strong>You should <a href=\"/contact\">schedule trailer repair</a> if:</strong>",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "list-schedule-pro-3",
                  "type": "prose-list",
                  "props": {
                    "ordered": false,
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "text": "Brake lights stop working repeatedly"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Multiple lighting systems fail"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Wiring appears damaged"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Electrical connectors show corrosion"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Fuses continue blowing"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Trailer lights work inconsistently"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-schedule",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Dependable Service From People Who Understand the Industry",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "schedule"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-schedule-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "If your trailer brake lights are not working, don't wait for a roadside inspection or safety issue to force repairs. You need service teams that respect your time, communicate clearly, and provide solutions that actually solve the problem. Whether you need electrical diagnostics, connector replacement, or full trailer repair, <a href=\"/locations/trailer-sales\">Sun State Trailers</a> is ready to help.",
